window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-d0232fd4f7e84c22"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"organize-a-semester-workspace\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">整理学期学习工作区</h1> <p>将分散的课程文件和截止日期整理为一个经过核验的系统。</p> <p>使用课程文件夹、教学大纲、作业说明、阅读材料、笔记和日历信息整理学期工作区，保留原件，并建立链接到官方来源的截止日期跟踪表。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>刚开始新学期、课程文件散落在各个课程文件夹和下载目录中的学生。</li> <li>需要根据官方材料核验日期的学期规划。</li> <li>需要保留原件并归档重复文件的工作区。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>在保留原始材料的前提下整理课程文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>创建带来源链接和冲突标记的截止日期跟踪表。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>整理我的学期工作区</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请按课程整理这些学期文件，并为官方课程材料、阅读材料、笔记、作业和已提交作业分别创建子文件夹。\n\n请：\n- 保留原始文件\n- 找出重复文件并将其归档\n- 统一文件命名方式\n- 创建课程索引\n- 根据教学大纲和作业说明建立截止日期跟踪表\n- 为每个截止日期附上其官方来源链接\n\n请核验每个日期；遇到冲突时标记出来，不要猜测。移动或重命名文件前，先向我展示拟议的结构。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"gather-official-course-sources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">收集官方课程来源</h2> <p>收集每门课的教学大纲、作业说明、阅读清单、课程日历和当前文件夹。区分官方课程材料、个人笔记和已提交的作业。</p> <p>整理任何内容之前，先让 ChatGPT 清点文件、找出重复项并展示拟议的文件夹结构。</p> <p><a id=\"build-the-workspace\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">建立工作区</h2> <p>实用的学期工作区可以包括：</p> <ul> <li>每门课一个文件夹</li> <li>分开存放官方材料、阅读材料、笔记、作业和已提交作业</li> <li>命名一致且便于搜索的文件</li> <li>包含重要文件链接的课程索引</li> <li>为每个日期标明来源的截止日期跟踪表</li> </ul> <p>保留原始文件；较旧的重复版本应归档，不要删除。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-deadlines-and-conflicts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">核验截止日期和冲突</h2> <p>对照教学大纲或作业说明核验每个截止日期。遇到日期冲突、时区缺失或提交要求不明确时，应标记出来，不要擅自选择一个答案。</p> <p>审阅拟议结构后，请分小批批准文件修改。收到新的官方课程材料时，再次检查索引和截止日期跟踪表。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"organize-a-semester-workspace\">Organize a semester workspace</h1> <p>Turn scattered course files and deadlines into one verified system.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with course folders, syllabi, assignment sheets, readings, notes, and calendar context to organize a semester workspace, preserve originals, and build a deadline tracker linked to official sources.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Students starting a new term with files spread across courses and downloads.</li> <li>Semester planning that needs dates verified against official materials.</li> <li>Workspaces that should preserve originals and archive duplicates.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>Organize course files while preserving original materials.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Build a deadline tracker with source links and conflict flags.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Organize My Semester Workspace</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Organize these semester files into a clear workspace by course, with subfolders for official course materials, readings, notes, assignments, and submitted work.\n\nPlease:\n- preserve the original files\n- identify and archive duplicates\n- use consistent file names\n- create a course index\n- build a deadline tracker from the syllabi and assignment sheets\n- link every deadline to its official source\n\nVerify every date and flag conflicts instead of guessing. Show me the proposed structure before moving or renaming anything.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"gather-official-course-sources\">Gather official course sources</h2> <p>Collect each syllabus, assignment sheet, reading list, course calendar, and current folder. Distinguish official course materials from personal notes and submitted work.</p> <p>Before organizing anything, ask ChatGPT to inventory the files, identify duplicates, and show the proposed folder structure.</p> <h2 id=\"build-the-workspace\">Build the workspace</h2> <p>A useful semester workspace should include:</p> <ul> <li>one folder per course</li> <li>separate locations for official materials, readings, notes, assignments, and submitted work</li> <li>consistent, searchable file names</li> <li>a course index with links to important files</li> <li>a deadline tracker with the source for every date</li> </ul> <p>Preserve original files and archive older duplicates rather than deleting them.</p> <h2 id=\"verify-deadlines-and-conflicts\">Verify deadlines and conflicts</h2> <p>Compare each deadline against the syllabus or assignment sheet. Flag conflicting dates, missing time zones, and unclear submission instructions instead of choosing one silently.</p> <p>After reviewing the proposed structure, approve file changes in small batches. Recheck the indexes and deadline tracker whenever new official materials arrive.</p>"};
